1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,654
A house stands some way
from a long, straight road.

2
00:00:04,054 --> 00:00:07,475
You could walk from the house
to the road along many paths.

3
00:00:07,475 --> 00:00:08,950
Some long, some short.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,680
Aarav wants the shortest one.

5
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:15,408
Which path is it, and how long is it,
if all we know is the house's position

6
00:00:15,408 --> 00:00:16,839
and the road's equation?

7
00:00:17,339 --> 00:00:19,424
One neat formula answers both.

8
00:00:19,424 --> 00:00:20,686
Let us find it.

9
00:00:21,336 --> 00:00:26,254
Here is the road, the line three x
plus four y minus twelve equals zero.

10
00:00:26,254 --> 00:00:29,287
The house is the point P, at five, four.

11
00:00:29,687 --> 00:00:34,504
Let a point Q slide along the road,
and watch the distance from P to Q.

12
00:00:34,904 --> 00:00:36,456
Far away, it is big.

13
00:00:36,456 --> 00:00:38,535
As Q comes closer, it shrinks.

14
00:00:38,535 --> 00:00:39,435
Seven.

15
00:00:39,109 --> 00:00:40,009
Five.

16
00:00:39,636 --> 00:00:40,793
Four point four.

17
00:00:40,793 --> 00:00:41,997
Three point nine.

18
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:44,285
Then it starts growing again.

19
00:00:44,285 --> 00:00:48,506
The smallest distance, three point
eight, comes exactly when PQ meets

20
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:50,309
the road at a right angle.

21
00:00:50,909 --> 00:00:55,491
So the distance of a point from a line
means the length of the perpendicular,

22
00:00:55,491 --> 00:00:57,324
from the point to the line.

23
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:02,276
To find that length without drawing,
write the line with everything on

24
00:01:02,276 --> 00:01:03,176
one side.

25
00:01:03,084 --> 00:01:05,437
A x plus B y plus C equals zero.

26
00:01:05,837 --> 00:01:09,540
Here, A is three, B is
four, and C is minus twelve.

27
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:11,040
Step one.

28
00:01:11,012 --> 00:01:13,862
From P, go straight down to the road.

29
00:01:13,862 --> 00:01:19,051
This vertical gap is the size of A
x one plus B y one plus C, over B.

30
00:01:19,801 --> 00:01:20,701
Step two.

31
00:01:20,564 --> 00:01:22,369
The perpendicular is shorter.

32
00:01:22,369 --> 00:01:26,288
Together with the vertical gap,
it makes a small right triangle.

33
00:01:27,038 --> 00:01:27,938
Step three.

34
00:01:27,886 --> 00:01:32,110
That small triangle has the same shape
as the road's own slope triangle.

35
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:34,618
Run four, rise three, long side five.

36
00:01:34,618 --> 00:01:37,514
So the perpendicular is
four fifths of the gap.

37
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:41,083
In general, B over the root
of A squared plus B squared.

38
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:42,733
Step four.

39
00:01:42,713 --> 00:01:43,855
The B's cancel.

40
00:01:43,855 --> 00:01:48,859
d is the size of A x one plus B y one
plus C, over the root of A squared

41
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:50,052
plus B squared.

42
00:01:50,802 --> 00:01:55,967
For our house, the top is fifteen plus
sixteen minus twelve, which is nineteen.

43
00:01:55,967 --> 00:01:57,387
The bottom is five.

44
00:01:57,387 --> 00:02:00,019
Nineteen over five is three point eight.

45
00:02:00,019 --> 00:02:00,926
It matches.

46
00:02:01,576 --> 00:02:02,547
Side by side.

47
00:02:02,547 --> 00:02:06,448
The distance of a point from a
line needs one point and the line.

48
00:02:06,848 --> 00:02:11,009
The distance between two parallel
lines is the same everywhere.

49
00:02:11,009 --> 00:02:16,440
With A x plus B y plus C one, and A
x plus B y plus C two, it is the size

50
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:19,561
of C one minus C two, over the same root.

51
00:02:20,161 --> 00:02:21,061
Your turn.

52
00:02:20,938 --> 00:02:22,967
A point lies on the line itself.

53
00:02:22,967 --> 00:02:25,131
What is its distance from the line?

54
00:02:25,131 --> 00:02:26,275
Pause and decide.

55
00:02:29,475 --> 00:02:30,375
Zero!

56
00:02:30,036 --> 00:02:34,466
For a point on the line, A x
one plus B y one plus C is zero.

57
00:02:34,466 --> 00:02:35,969
So the top is zero.

58
00:02:36,619 --> 00:02:37,669
Remember this.

59
00:02:37,669 --> 00:02:40,180
The shortest path is the perpendicular.

60
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:45,076
Its length is the size of A x one plus
B y one plus C, over root A squared

61
00:02:45,076 --> 00:02:46,233
plus B squared.

62
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:48,332
One habit to keep.

63
00:02:48,332 --> 00:02:51,802
The line must equal zero
before you use the formula.

64
00:02:52,202 --> 00:02:57,595
Three x plus four y equals ten becomes
three x plus four y minus ten equals

65
00:02:57,595 --> 00:02:58,495
zero.

66
00:02:58,229 --> 00:03:00,631
So C is minus ten, not ten.

67
00:03:01,231 --> 00:03:02,131
Quick one.

68
00:03:02,065 --> 00:03:06,377
How far is the origin from the line
three x plus four y equals ten?

69
00:03:06,377 --> 00:03:07,556
Pause and think.

70
00:03:10,756 --> 00:03:11,656
Two!

71
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,731
Put in zero, zero.

72
00:03:12,731 --> 00:03:16,050
The top is the size of
minus ten, which is ten.

73
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:17,630
Ten over five is two.

74
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,970
Now, one worked example.

75
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:24,830
Find the distance of the point three,
one from the line twelve x minus

76
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:26,949
five y plus eight equals zero.

77
00:03:27,449 --> 00:03:28,349
Step one.

78
00:03:28,287 --> 00:03:30,033
Read off A, B and C.

79
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:32,331
Twelve, minus five, and eight.

80
00:03:33,081 --> 00:03:33,981
Step two.

81
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:34,733
Top.

82
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:37,638
Twelve times three, minus
five times one, plus eight.

83
00:03:37,638 --> 00:03:39,004
That is thirty nine.

84
00:03:39,754 --> 00:03:40,654
Step three.

85
00:03:40,634 --> 00:03:41,534
Bottom.

86
00:03:41,266 --> 00:03:44,568
The root of one hundred
forty four plus twenty five.

87
00:03:44,568 --> 00:03:47,133
The root of one sixty nine is thirteen.

88
00:03:47,883 --> 00:03:48,783
Step four.

89
00:03:48,617 --> 00:03:50,610
Thirty nine over thirteen is three.

90
00:03:50,610 --> 00:03:52,872
The point is three units from the line.

91
00:03:53,522 --> 00:03:54,984
Now, the exam trap.

92
00:03:55,334 --> 00:04:00,013
Find the distance between three x
plus four y minus two equals zero, and

93
00:04:00,013 --> 00:04:02,857
six x plus eight y plus one equals zero.

94
00:04:02,857 --> 00:04:04,998
Many students get three fifths.

95
00:04:05,398 --> 00:04:08,226
But the x and y parts must match first.

96
00:04:08,226 --> 00:04:09,867
Halve the second line.

97
00:04:09,867 --> 00:04:13,119
Three x plus four y plus
one half equals zero.

98
00:04:13,119 --> 00:04:15,772
Minus two minus one half, over five.

99
00:04:15,772 --> 00:04:17,527
The answer is one half.

100
00:04:18,177 --> 00:04:19,581
Where is this asked?

101
00:04:19,581 --> 00:04:23,851
In JEE Main, for example in April
twenty nineteen: lines parallel to a

102
00:04:23,851 --> 00:04:26,858
given line, at a set
distance from the origin.

103
00:04:27,458 --> 00:04:28,601
Exam level now.

104
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:32,553
Two points on the x axis are at
distance four from this line.

105
00:04:32,553 --> 00:04:34,946
Find the sum of their x coordinates.

106
00:04:34,946 --> 00:04:36,137
Pause and solve.

107
00:04:41,537 --> 00:04:43,158
The answer is B.

108
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:44,058
Six.

109
00:04:44,298 --> 00:04:47,090
A point on the x axis is h, zero.

110
00:04:47,090 --> 00:04:51,508
Its distance is the size of
four h minus twelve, over five.

111
00:04:52,008 --> 00:04:53,914
Set that equal to four.

112
00:04:53,914 --> 00:04:58,129
So four h minus twelve is
plus twenty, or minus twenty.

113
00:04:58,629 --> 00:05:02,285
That gives h equals eight,
or h equals minus two.

114
00:05:02,285 --> 00:05:03,726
Their sum is six.

115
00:05:04,326 --> 00:05:05,866
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:05,866 --> 00:05:07,449
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:10,649 --> 00:05:12,835
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:05:13,235 --> 00:05:14,135
One.

119
00:05:13,732 --> 00:05:18,066
How far is the origin from the line
five x plus twelve y equals twenty

120
00:05:18,066 --> 00:05:18,966
six?

121
00:05:19,463 --> 00:05:20,363
Two.

122
00:05:19,915 --> 00:05:23,889
Why is the shortest path from a
point to a line always perpendicular?

123
00:05:24,789 --> 00:05:25,689
Three.

124
00:05:25,397 --> 00:05:30,492
What is the distance between x plus y
equals one, and x plus y equals three?

125
00:05:31,592 --> 00:05:36,123
Next time, a new chapter: slice an
ice cream cone four different ways,

126
00:05:36,123 --> 00:05:38,129
and four famous curves appear.

127
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,596
Sections of a cone, and the circle.
